Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `date`: filter rows to the two calendar‑year windows (2019‑01‑01 – 2019‑12‑31 and 2020‑01‑01 – 2020‑12‑31) and for any additional grouping by week or year.  
• `sub_region_2`: identify the five New York City counties: Bronx County, Queens County, Kings County, New York County, and Richmond County.  
• `sub_region_1` / `sub_region_1_code`: extra safety check that the rows belong to New York State (`sub_region_1 = 'New York'`, `sub_region_1_code = 'US-NY'`).  
• `country_region_code`: keep only United States rows (`country_region_code = 'US'`).  
• `symptom_anosmia`: the weekly Google‑search index we need to average and compare between 2019 and 2020.  
(All other columns are not needed for this task.)

Typical filter conditions  
```
country_region_code = 'US'
sub_region_1        = 'New York'
sub_region_2        IN ('Bronx County','Queens County','Kings County',
                        'New York County','Richmond County')
DATE(date) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
```  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑solution queries (each limited to 20 rows where appropriate) showing how one could progressively arrive at the required percentage‑change figure.

